+// ExecuteCloseTabsCommand: `get_tabs`, keeping only the tabs this window draws
+// when it returns more than one. A shift-click selects a RANGE of the model,
+// which can hold tabs this window does not draw -- another workspace's, an
+// open pinned item's page (E15c). A close of several tabs closes only the
+// drawn ones, as a move does (E13); one tab is closed as asked.
+base::RepeatingCallback<std::vector<tabs::TabInterface*>()> DrawnTabsOnly(
+    const TabStripModelDelegate* delegate,
+    base::RepeatingCallback<std::vector<tabs::TabInterface*>()> get_tabs);
